      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 137, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced course catalog table: an alternative catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags, section flags, meeting time/place), plus subject-offering reference columns (SO_SUBJECT_ID, SO_TERM_CODE, SO_TERM_DESCRIPTION, SO_CLUSTER_TYPE) linking catalog records to registrar subject offerings.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEGREE_PROGRAM\", \"desc\": \"19 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ENROLLABLE\", \"desc\": \"11 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"Subject attribute lookup table decoding attribute codes attached to subjects: academic attributes (type 'A') such as calculus/science prerequisites and HASS-D/HASS category codes, and non-academic program flags (type 'N') such as ROTC, ESG, Concourse, co-op, and listener rules. Provides short, full, and reporting descriptions per code. Overlaps with CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE on HASS-family codes (HD1-HD5, HDL, HE, HA, HH, HS) but differs in scope: SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE covers all subject attribute types with one description variant per code, while CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE covers only HASS attribute codes with separate registration-form and bulletin descriptions plus attribute-group (H/G) classification. Catalog subject records' GIR_ATTRIBUTE codes all resolve against SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject category lookup table with category name and description. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_IAP_SCHEDULE\", \"desc\": \"10 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\", \"desc\": \"Library course instructor table recording instructors of courses with library reserve materials, including course name, instructor name, department (in 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' format), assignment date range, and library organizational unit/branch. Referenced by LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY; instructor names resolve to person records via INSTRUCTOR_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERM_PARAMETER\", \"desc\": \"Term parameter reference table holding exactly three rows that identify the SIS current term, previous term, and upcoming term, each with its term code, description, start/end dates and the last day before the next term. Used to resolve relative term references ('C', 'P', 'F') to concrete term codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Independent Activities Period (IAP) subject detail table: one row per IAP activity offered in a January term, with activity title/description, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, fee, prerequisites, preregistration deadline, cancellation and multiple-session flags, and foreign keys to category, sponsor, session, and person tables.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ROOMS\", \"desc\": \"Facilities room inventory table: one row per physical room with building/floor keys, room identifiers, use classifications (major/minor use), organization assignment, area in square meters, access level, and geographic coordinates. Joins to FCLT_BUILDING via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY; referenced by COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.MEET_PLACE via FCLT_ROOM_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SELECTOR\", \"desc\": \"16 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Library reserve material detail bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, course instructors, and material status per term. Used to count reserved materials per subject and to filter by library material status (e.g. 'U').\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_FACULTY_ROSTER\", \"desc\": \"HR faculty roster table: one row per faculty member keyed by MIT_ID with name components, terminal degree, appointment type, job/position titles across HR, administrative, and directory organization units, endowed chair, and emeritus status. Used for faculty appointment and credential analysis; joins to EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MIT_ID for contact details.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_HOLIDAY_CLOSING_CALENDAR\", \"desc\": \"4 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_GROUPING\", \"desc\": \"7 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"TIME_MONTH\", \"desc\": \"Month-level (fiscal period) time dimension table: one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, mapping each month to its fiscal year/quarter, calendar year/period/month, academic year and academic term, and financial aid year, with period start/end dates and current/previous/closing period flags. Covers fiscal years 1996-2035 (640 periods). Joins to TIME_DAY via FISCAL_PERIOD for day-level detail, to TIME_QUARTER via FY_QUARTER_CODE for quarter attributes, and to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL via ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE for term attributes; used for fiscal-period grouping and month-level calendar statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"CIS lookup table decoding HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute codes used in course catalog subject records. Each code (e.g. 'HA', 'HH', 'HS', 'HE', 'HD1'-'HD5', 'HDL', and combined codes like 'HA,HH') maps to two description variants: the description shown on the registration form and the shorter description printed in the bulletin, plus the CIS attribute group ('H' = HASS_ATTRIBUTE for students entering Fall 2010 or later, 'G' = GIR_ATTRIBUTE for students entering prior to Fall 2010) with a group note, and icon display attributes. Catalog tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG) join to this lookup via HASS_ATTRIBUTE. Note: a code can appear once per attribute group (e.g. 'HE' exists in both group H and group G), so joins on HASS_ATTRIBUTE alone may produce multiple matching rows.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject person table: one row per person associated with an IAP activity, recording the person's role in the activity (Activity leader, Session leader, Contact person), MIT affiliation type, name, location, email, organization, and title. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON_KEY; used to analyze activity leadership and person roles, e.g. enrollment capacity statistics per person role.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING_HIST\", \"desc\": \"Historical facilities building snapshot table: one row per building per fiscal period (FISCAL_PERIOD in YYYYMM format, covering 201505-201906, 48 periods, ~255 buildings), preserving each building's attributes over time: identifiers and names, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, site, campus sector, access level, building type, ownership type, use, occupancy class, height, cost center/collector references, coordinates, and number of rooms. Used for fiscal-period building history analysis (area/room-count trends, dispersion statistics across historical records); use FCLT_BUILDING for the current snapshot. Date columns (DATE_BUILT/DATE_ACQUIRED/DATE_OCCUPIED) are stored in MM/DD/YYYY format; FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1 is the variant storing them in DD-MON-YY format.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SESSION\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject session table: session-level details of IAP activities including session title, description, location, date, start/end times, and sequence. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SESSION_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject sponsor table listing sponsors of IAP activities with sponsor name and type. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"IR_INSTITUTION\", \"desc\": \"13 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Space assignment detail fact table: one row per physical room assigned to a space unit, with building/floor/space-unit/space-usage keys, room identifiers (building-room number and name, room number), room square footage, room counter, and building component. Used to count rooms per space unit or per building, and to analyze room size and usage distribution. Joins to SPACE_UNIT via SPACE_UNIT_KEY, FCLT_BUILDING via BUILDING_KEY, SPACE_FLOOR via FLOOR_KEY, and SPACE_USAGE via SPACE_USAGE_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"OPA_PERSON_CURRENT\", \"desc\": \"Current-person snapshot table from the OPA (Office of People Analytics) feed: one row per current person keyed by MIT_ID with name components, email, HR job attributes (job id/title, admin employee type, HR department, org unit and position titles, payroll rank), faculty flag, employment percent, privacy flags, sabbatical begin/end dates, and personnel subarea. Used for HR/appointment analysis of current people; carries no office phone or office location.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_2597\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the description of the academic year, the department name, the average total units for all subjects offered by that department in terms that match that academic year and have a term status indicator of 'P', and the deviation of each department's average total units from the overall average total units for that academic year? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3280\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2019FA term that have total units greater than 1, show the subject title, the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the academic year, the subject ID, the department name, and the running sum of total units within each school ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4231\", \"desc\": \"For each department that both offered subjects in the current SIS term and is a degree-granting department that offered subjects in the term '2016SP', list the department code, offering department name, subject title, responsible faculty name, term description, academic year description, total number of subjects offered per department in the current term, department name, number of subjects offered in 2016SP, and total units for those subjects in 2016SP. Include all columns in the order: department code, offering department name, subject title, responsible faculty name, term description, academic year description, total number of subjects offered per department in the current term, department name, number of subjects offered in 2016SP, and total units for those subjects in 2016SP. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4756\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3867\", \"desc\": \"For each subject in a department where the school code and subject title are not null, and for each subject offered in the 2022FA term with total units greater than the average for that term, display the subject code, subject code description, department name, subject title, the number of subjects in the same department, the subject ID, the term description, and the running sum of total units for that academic year, ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3644\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the 2012SU term with a total of 1 unit, show the subject title from the summary, the course number from the offered table, the subject title from the offered summary, the department name from the summary, the offer department name from the offered summary, the row number within each department name group ordered by subject title from the summary, and for each department, also provide the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student). List the results ordered by department name and row number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3493\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook, show the subject code, subject number, department name, subject title, term description, total units, the average subject enrollment number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by department code and ordered by total units, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number of the course within each department ordered by subject code. List the results in order by department name, subject code, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2580\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, provide the department name, academic year, the number of subjects offered that are not repeatable for credit and are offered in the fall term, and classify the department as 'HIGH_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% more such subjects than the average across all departments for that year, 'LOW_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% fewer, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1302\", \"desc\": \"For each course offered by a degree-granting department in the School of Engineering, except for the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department, in the 2007 academic year, what is the course key, course name, department name, the number of catalog subjects, the total units for those subjects, and for each department, include a grand total for all courses in the format of (null, null, department name, total subjects, total units)? Additionally, for each such department, what is the total number of units for courses in the \\\"Engineering\\\" or \\\"Non-MIT\\\" schools (where the total units for the department is greater than 1000 and the department is not \\\"Political Science\\\"), and how many distinct courses did the department offer in the most recent academic year available? Present the results as: course key, course name, department name, number of catalog subjects, total units for those subjects, department total units, and number of distinct courses in the latest year, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1023\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year where the Mathematics department has at least one unique subject with subject enrollment number greater than 10, what are the academic year, academic year description, department name, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, variance of total units, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of total units for subjects offered in the fall term that are not variable units and are offered by the Mathematics department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_41\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, provide the academic year description and calculate the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered in terms that are not the current term, have a term status indicator of 'P', are offered by the Mathematics department, and are full term subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2924\", \"desc\": \"For degree-granting courses in the School of Engineering, show the course description, department name, subject title, and the subject's grade type description, but only include those courses where the total units for the subject exceed the average total units for that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4305\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subjects offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" that have the highest number of enrolled students, display each subject's offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, the number of enrolled students, and the rank of each subject within its offering department (ordered by subject offered key), but only include subjects where the offering department is among those that, in the term with code '2022SU', had an average total units for their subjects greater than the average total units for all subjects offered in that term. List the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, term description, number of enrolled students, and the rank within the department, in that order, and order the results by department name and number of enrolled students descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3904\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_104\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2022 that are printed in the bulletin and belong to the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject title, department name, total units, and the difference between the total units of each subject and the average total units for Mathematics subjects in 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3163\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting and the total units are greater than 6, provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units offered, and the number of courses where the design units are at least 3. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1049\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for its subjects in regular terms that are not the current term, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year (considering only departments that have more than five subjects offered in 2022, are degree-granting, and are not the Chemistry department)? Show the department name, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for regular non-current terms, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) for 2022. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3248\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units that are also offered in the library by the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each subject within its department ordered by subject code, the number of enrolled students, offering department name, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4061\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, show the department name, academic year, academic year description, and the geometric mean of the total units for all subjects offered by the department in regular terms with total units greater than zero, along with, for each academic building where these subjects are held and which has rooms larger than 40 square meters, the building name, the average, range, and variance of the room areas, as well as the total assignable area of the building and the year the building was built. The results are ordered by department name, academic year (descending), and room area range (descending). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_359\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, what is the total number of lecture units for all subjects offered in regular terms by the Mathematics department (Course 18), where at least 60% of those subjects are undergraduate-level (HGN_DESC = 'Undergraduate'), considering only those academic years where the total lecture units are more than one standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) above the mean total lecture units across all academic years? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4130\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012 that also have a section ID of 0 and a cluster type of 'S', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the total number of subjects offered by each department in that year, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the department name from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, the term start date from ACADEMIC_TERMS, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED. List the results in order by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1301\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, where the maximum number of total units for any Mathematics (Course 18) subject offered in that year is greater than 9 and there are more than 5 Mathematics subjects offered in the fall term, what are the academic year, the maximum total units, the corresponding term description, the subject title, the academic year description, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in library subjects offered during terms in that year, and the average number of equivalent subjects for those library subjects? List the results in order of academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4911\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 subjects offered by departments in the School of Engineering with the highest maximum enrolled students (considering the current and next 2 rows ordered by subject key), display each subject's title, total units, department full name, row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the department that offered the subject. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4515\", \"desc\": \"For each department, academic year, activity title, and sponsor name where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the maximum enrollment for the activity is greater than 10, provide the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, activity title, sponsor name, number of unique activities, minimum fee, and the sponsor type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4448\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the department name, the highest total units among its subjects with exactly 12 units in the Fall Term 2024-2025, and for each course in that department that was offered in 2022 and has at least one required or optional textbook and has total units greater than the average for such courses, show the course's subject code, subject number, subject title, the term description, the textbook material key, the textbook material status key, and the row number within the department ordered by subject code. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5103\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3901\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2398\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4234\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees and offered subjects in the term '2016SP', and is also among the top 5 offering departments in the 'Engineering' school with the most 12-unit courses, list the department code, department name, the number of subjects offered, the total units for those subjects, the offering department name, the number of qualifying 12-unit courses, and the course number and description of the most recently added 12-unit course in each department. For each department, also include a grand total row for the number of subjects and total units in the format (department code, null, total subjects, total units, ...). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3635\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3273\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering with a total of 12 units, display the course number, course description, subject title, total units, offering department name, the row number of the course within its offering department ordered by course number, and the dense rank of the subject (considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by total units) if available. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3311\", \"desc\": \"For each course that has more than 0 enrolled students and a material status key of 'U', list the course number, course number description, number of enrolled students, reserve catalog key, and the dense rank over the material status key ordered by material status key, along with the department name, the range, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units of courses offered by that department (considering only courses offered this year with non-null total units). Present the results ordered by course number and course number description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2158\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 2022 academic year by a degree-granting department, specifically in the Department of Mathematics (Course 18) and excluding subjects offered by the Department of Physics, provide the subject ID, subject title, department name, the number of enrolled students, the total number of lecture units, and, for each subject, indicate whether it is also offered as a joint subject with another department. Additionally, show the range and variance of the total units for letter graded subjects offered this year in the Mathematics department. List the results in order of subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2210\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code in degree-granting departments where the department is Mathematics, and for subjects offered in the academic year 2024 that are also present in the CIS course catalog and are in the Mathematics department, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, rank of the subject code within each school name group ordered by subject code, subject ID, subject number, subject short title, subject title, lecture units, lab units, total units, grade type, grade rule, the minimum total units value over each department code group, and the subject description from the CIS course catalog, ordered by school name, rank, and subject number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2240\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the 'Engineering' school with total units greater than 0 and only for subjects in the 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' department (Course 6), show the subject title, total units, department name, course description, and dense rank over the offer department code ordered by offer department code, along with the first name, last name, department name, student year, corresponding department's full name, administrative department name, and the average department phone number in a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by the administrative department name and ordered by the student's first name, for students whose department is '6' and whose department name is 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci', where the subject's offer department code matches the student's department. Then, for each offer department code, provide the maximum total units among these subjects and the count of distinct student years among the matched students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4387\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the School of Engineering with total student enrollment in its courses greater than the average total enrollment across all Engineering departments (and with total enrollment greater than 50), display the department name, the total number of students enrolled in its courses, and the highest average total units for subjects it has ever offered in a regular academic term, listing the results in descending order of total enrollment. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3727\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, or for each department that offered more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of tip materials. List the department code, department name, department full name, number of subjects offered, total number of enrolled students, and total number of tip materials in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5150\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects in the course catalog are offered in the spring term, have a total of at least 6 units, are taught by faculty who are responsible for at least one subject with more than 0 enrolled students according to the subject offered summary, and are in the Mathematics department (Course 18)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4724\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the library in the Mathematics department during regular terms, show the subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, and the maximum total units for each row and the next two rows in order of subject ID. Additionally, for the corresponding offering department and school, provide the number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ' and the minimum total units for those subjects. Also, include the department phone number and the school name for the offering department, and display the responsible faculty name for each subject. The columns should be shown in the following order: subject title, number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, academic year, subject short title, maximum total units for each row and the next two rows, number of unique subjects with course material status 'RQ', minimum total units for those subjects, department phone number, school name, and responsible faculty name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1212\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department (Course 18), provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student), the number of graduate students in the department, and the most recent warehouse load date for those students, considering only departments that are degree granting and students whose year is 'G'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3237\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2958\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year, among subjects that are not repeatable, what is the average, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by each department? List the academic year, department name, average enrollment, variance, and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), ordered by variance descending. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3632\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", show the subject title, subject key, offer department name, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, subject ID, academic year, term description, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row, ordered by offer department name and academic year. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_fa33761c4d374a70b02cfdff",
      "name": "semantic_search",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"count\": 137, \"items_by_type\": {\"table\": [{\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"Student-facing department lookup table with department code, name, full name, and school attribution (code and name). Similar in content to SIS_DEPARTMENT but oriented to student information systems reporting; joins to offering tables via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\", \"desc\": \"SIS course description table: catalog descriptions of courses with department and school attribution, course level (undergraduate/graduate), degree-granting flag, graduate level, CIP program code, and effective from/thru terms. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via COURSE = SUBJECT_CODE/COURSE_NUMBER and to SIS_DEPARTMENT via DEPARTMENT = DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"STUDENT_DEGREE_PROGRAM\", \"desc\": \"19 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Student directory table: one row per student with name components, full name, office location and phone, email address, department code and department name, and student year. The DEPARTMENT column stores the academic department code and joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE, enabling per-department student counts.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy table: one row per department/lab/center (DLC) under the 'Standard Hierarchy' hierarchy type, recording the DLC key/code/name and its five-level hierarchy path from the institute root (level 1 'All Departments') through executive areas down to the DLC's placement, with each level's code and name (null for levels deeper than the DLC's position). Joins to HR_ORG_UNIT and FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY; used to report or filter the master-hierarchy placement (school/area path) of a DLC, and as a DLC scope filter when only DLCs present in the standard hierarchy should be included.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_FACULTY_ROSTER\", \"desc\": \"HR faculty roster table: one row per faculty member keyed by MIT_ID with name components, terminal degree, appointment type, job/position titles across HR, administrative, and directory organization units, endowed chair, and emeritus status. Used for faculty appointment and credential analysis; joins to EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MIT_ID for contact details.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS administrative department table with administrative department code/name, phone area code and phone number, and clearing cost collector. Joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT via SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE for department contact information.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Section-level subject offering fact table: one row per subject section offered in a term, with section flags (master/lecture/lab/recitation/design), cluster information, offering department and school, responsible faculty, meeting time/place, and enrollment numbers at section, subject, and cluster level. Linked to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (subject level) via SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY/COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY and to SUBJECT_SUMMARY via SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with unit key/ID/title, unit level classification (ALL MIT, TOP LEVEL, DEPARTMENTS, SUB DEPARTMENT, ORGANIZATION LEVEL, NON HIERARCHY ORG UNITS), HR department identifiers and name variants (short, long, alphabetical), organization hierarchy area names (school area, top level, root), the full HR hierarchy path levels 1-7 (each with ID, sort order, and name), and DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME cross-references to departments/labs/centers. Joined from FCLT_ORGANIZATION and MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY to attach HR department attributes (title, level, department name, long name, hierarchy path) to facilities organizations and DLCs; a single DLC_KEY can map to multiple HR org unit rows, so joins via DLC_KEY may fan out.\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization dimension table: one row per organization in the institute's hierarchical organization tree (levels 1-6, from institute-wide down to sub-units), with organization identifiers and names, parent and major-organization attribution, hierarchy level, assignable-space flag, course number for academic departments, description, DLC (department/lab/center) key and name, and cross-references to HR organization units. Parent of SPACE_UNIT (space assigned to organizations) and referenced by FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY for room occupancy attribution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT\", \"desc\": \"Department parent lookup table: one row per department code (D_CODE) with its department name and the identity of its direct parent department (parent ID, parent D code, parent name). A flattened single-level parent view of the department tree; use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY when the full multi-level hierarchy path of a DLC is required. D_CODE matches MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY/DLC_CODE and other DLC key columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Library subject offered table: subjects offered per term that appear in library reserve processing, with subject identity, course number, offering department/school, responsible faculty, and enrollment count. Parent of LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS\", \"desc\": \"Master department hierarchy link table: one row per association between a department/lab/center (DLC) and a linked administrative object, classified by link type (Standard Funds Center, PCMIT-0 Profit Center, New/Old Org. Unit, Facilities Org., Student Systems Unit, NIMBUS B.A.G.). A DLC may hold many links of several types. Joins to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY via DLC_KEY; used to map DLCs to their fund centers, profit centers, facilities organizations, and other linked object codes.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) subject offered table: one row per subject offered in a term within the textbook program scope, with subject identity, offering department/school, responsible faculty, enrollment count, and a flag indicating whether the subject has no course material. Parent of TIP_DETAIL via TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Employee directory table: one row per institute employee with MIT ID, legal and preferred name components, directory/primary titles, HR department number and name, office location and office phone, email address, personal URL, and Kerberos name. Used to resolve responsible faculty contact details (full name, email, office phone) for subject offerings via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID, and to link employees to Moira mailing list membership via MIT_ID = MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR\", \"desc\": \"Library course instructor table recording instructors of courses with library reserve materials, including course name, instructor name, department (in 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' format), assignment date range, and library organizational unit/branch. Referenced by LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL via LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR_KEY; instructor names resolve to person records via INSTRUCTOR_NAME = SE_PERSON.FULL_NAME.\"}, {\"id\": \"OPA_PERSON_CURRENT\", \"desc\": \"Current-person snapshot table from the OPA (Office of People Analytics) feed: one row per current person keyed by MIT_ID with name components, email, HR job attributes (job id/title, admin employee type, HR department, org unit and position titles, payroll rank), faculty flag, employment percent, privacy flags, sabbatical begin/end dates, and personnel subarea. Used for HR/appointment analysis of current people; carries no office phone or office location.\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\", \"desc\": \"SIS subject code lookup table mapping subject codes and course numbers to their descriptions, departments, and schools. Used to resolve subject code descriptions and to link courses to departments via DEPARTMENT_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW\", \"desc\": \"Newer HR organization unit dimension table: one row per HR organization unit with the same unit/department identity and hierarchy-path structure as HR_ORG_UNIT (unit key/ID/title/level, HR department code and name variants, school-area/top-level/root names, hierarchy path levels 1-5, DLC_KEY) but a shallower hierarchy path (levels 6-7 absent), no HR_DEPARTMENT_ID and no DLC_NAME column, and an extra HR_DEPARTMENT_ABBR abbreviation column. Holds more unit rows than HR_ORG_UNIT (691 vs 641, including units absent from HR_ORG_UNIT); use HR_ORG_UNIT when DLC_NAME or the deeper hierarchy path is required, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW for the newer unit coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"CIS course catalog table: an alternative course catalog source with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags), keyed by academic year, term code, and subject identity. Joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE via DEPARTMENT_CODE for subject code resolution.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_SUPERVISOR_USAGE\", \"desc\": \"Space supervisor usage fact table: one row per supervisor (MIT_ID) recording how much space they supervise and for how many departments: department count, department DLC key list (comma-separated when multiple), number of supervisees, supervised square footage, research volume, and derived ratio measures (sqft per supervisee, sqft per research volume, research volume per sqft). Joins to SPACE_UNIT and other DLC-carrying tables via DEPT_NAMES = DLC_KEY (only single-department rows match); used for supervisor space-usage and research-volume statistics per department/DLC.\"}, {\"id\": \"FAC_ORGANIZATION\", \"desc\": \"Facilities organization snapshot table with the same hierarchical organization structure as FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization identifiers, parent/major organization, level, assignable flag, course number, description, HR cross-references) but keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY and carrying D_CODE instead of DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME. Contains fewer organizations than FCLT_ORGANIZATION; used as an alternative organization dimension in FAC_* family queries.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"CIS lookup table decoding HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute codes used in course catalog subject records. Each code (e.g. 'HA', 'HH', 'HS', 'HE', 'HD1'-'HD5', 'HDL', and combined codes like 'HA,HH') maps to two description variants: the description shown on the registration form and the shorter description printed in the bulletin, plus the CIS attribute group ('H' = HASS_ATTRIBUTE for students entering Fall 2010 or later, 'G' = GIR_ATTRIBUTE for students entering prior to Fall 2010) with a group note, and icon display attributes. Catalog tables (COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, CIS_COURSE_CATALOG, DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG) join to this lookup via HASS_ATTRIBUTE. Note: a code can appear once per attribute group (e.g. 'HE' exists in both group H and group G), so joins on HASS_ATTRIBUTE alone may produce multiple matching rows.\"}, {\"id\": \"SPACE_UNIT\", \"desc\": \"Space unit dimension table: one row per space unit (an organizational space-assignment unit such as a department, program, or office that receives space allocation), with space unit key/code, space unit name, the facilities organization it belongs to, and DLC key. Bridges FCLT_ORGANIZATION (organization attribution) and SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to the space unit); used to group room counts and space statistics by space unit.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE\", \"desc\": \"Subject attribute lookup table decoding attribute codes attached to subjects: academic attributes (type 'A') such as calculus/science prerequisites and HASS-D/HASS category codes, and non-academic program flags (type 'N') such as ROTC, ESG, Concourse, co-op, and listener rules. Provides short, full, and reporting descriptions per code. Overlaps with CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE on HASS-family codes (HD1-HD5, HDL, HE, HA, HH, HS) but differs in scope: SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE covers all subject attribute types with one description variant per code, while CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE covers only HASS attribute codes with separate registration-form and bulletin descriptions plus attribute-group (H/G) classification. Catalog subject records' GIR_ATTRIBUTE codes all resolve against SUBJECT_ATTRIBUTE_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\", \"desc\": \"Extended academic term dimension table covering all terms known to the warehouse (a superset of ACADEMIC_TERMS, including terms without full status tracking). Shares term calendar attributes (term code, dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, registration and class dates) but does not carry IS_REGULAR_TERM, TERM_STATUS, ADD_DATE or DROP_DATE columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject category lookup table with category name and description. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_CATEGORY_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\"}, {\"id\": \"MIT_HOLIDAY_CLOSING_CALENDAR\", \"desc\": \"4 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced employee directory table: an alternative employee feed keyed by MIT_ID with name components, employee group/type, additional/dual appointment flags, office location and phone, HR organization unit id/title, directory/primary titles, email address, and personal URL. Same person domain as EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY but from the Drupal source system and without Kerberos/preferred-name columns; used as an alternative employee lookup when Drupal-sourced attributes (employee group, appointment flags, HR org unit) are needed.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject person table: one row per person associated with an IAP activity, recording the person's role in the activity (Activity leader, Session leader, Contact person), MIT affiliation type, name, location, email, organization, and title. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_PERSON_KEY; used to analyze activity leadership and person roles, e.g. enrollment capacity statistics per person role.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Independent Activities Period (IAP) subject detail table: one row per IAP activity offered in a January term, with activity title/description, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, fee, prerequisites, preregistration deadline, cancellation and multiple-session flags, and foreign keys to category, sponsor, session, and person tables.\"}, {\"id\": \"LIBRARY_RESERVE_MATRL_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Library reserve material detail bridge table linking reserve catalog items, library subject offerings, course instructors, and material status per term. Used to count reserved materials per subject and to filter by library material status (e.g. 'U').\"}, {\"id\": \"DRUPAL_COURSE_CATALOG\", \"desc\": \"Drupal-sourced course catalog table: an alternative catalog feed with the same subject attribute structure as COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED (units, grading, requirement attributes, offering flags, section flags, meeting time/place), plus subject-offering reference columns (SO_SUBJECT_ID, SO_TERM_CODE, SO_TERM_DESCRIPTION, SO_CLUSTER_TYPE) linking catalog records to registrar subject offerings.\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY\", \"desc\": \"Bridge table mapping facilities organizations to their department/lab/center (DLC) keys: one row per organization-DLC key assignment. Used to filter organizations that have a non-null DLC key assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION (via FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY or DLC_KEY) for DLC-level facility and room statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR\", \"desc\": \"IAP subject sponsor table listing sponsors of IAP activities with sponsor name and type. Referenced by IAP_SUBJECT_DETAIL via IAP_SUBJECT_SPONSOR_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"IR_INSTITUTION\", \"desc\": \"13 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"TIP_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Textbook Information Program (TIP) detail table linking subjects offered in a term to their course textbook materials: material key, material status (e.g. 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options), ISBN, and record count. Used to determine whether subjects have required textbooks and to count course materials per status.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIME_MONTH\", \"desc\": \"Month-level (fiscal period) time dimension table: one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, mapping each month to its fiscal year/quarter, calendar year/period/month, academic year and academic term, and financial aid year, with period start/end dates and current/previous/closing period flags. Covers fiscal years 1996-2035 (640 periods). Joins to TIME_DAY via FISCAL_PERIOD for day-level detail, to TIME_QUARTER via FY_QUARTER_CODE for quarter attributes, and to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL via ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE for term attributes; used for fiscal-period grouping and month-level calendar statistics.\"}, {\"id\": \"SE_PERSON\", \"desc\": \"Person master table keyed by MIT_ID with Kerberos name, full name, payroll rank, position title, active flag, office location, organization, name components, and employee type. A general-purpose person dimension covering employees with payroll/position attributes; narrower contact information than EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY (no email or phone).\"}, {\"id\": \"FCLT_BUILDING\", \"desc\": \"Facilities building inventory table: one row per physical building with building number/name, type (e.g. ACADEMIC), ownership, use, occupancy class, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates (built/acquired/occupied), site and geographic coordinates. Parent of FCLT_ROOMS via FCLT_BUILDING_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIP\", \"desc\": \"Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) lookup table: one row per six-digit CIP program code, classifying instructional programs into a two-digit category and a four-digit series, with program/category/four-digit titles, a change note, the CIP revision version year (1990/2000/2010/2020), and the warehouse load date. Joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs, categories, and schools/departments; CIP_WITH_VERSION is the multi-version variant keeping every revision of each program code.\"}, {\"id\": \"CIP_WITH_VERSION\", \"desc\": \"Versioned Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) lookup table: one row per CIP program code per revision version year (1990/2000/2010/2020), preserving the historical classification of each program across CIP revisions. Carries the same program/category/four-digit code and title attributes as CIP plus a surrogate key, but no NOTE column and fewer distinct program codes than CIP. Joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE (matching more course rows than CIP because a program code can appear under several versions); use CIP when one row per program code is required.\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_IAP_SCHEDULE\", \"desc\": \"10 columns in total\"}, {\"id\": \"MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL\", \"desc\": \"Moira mailing-list/group membership detail table: one row per list member with the list key, list owner key, member login, member full name, member MIT ID, last update date, and a counter. Used to find which Moira lists a person belongs to (joining EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY on MOIRA_LIST_MEMBER_MIT_ID = MIT_ID), and to decode list identity via MOIRA_LIST and ownership via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER.\"}, {\"id\": \"TIME_DAY\", \"desc\": \"Day-level time dimension table mapping each calendar date to fiscal year/period, calendar year/period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description the day belongs to. Used to attach calendar attributes to terms and activities.\"}], \"metric\": [{\"id\": \"dw_4812\", \"desc\": \"From the top 10 combinations of department name, subject code, and course number (where the department is degree granting and the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2) with the highest number of unique library subjects offered, display the department name, subject code, number of subject codes, minimum department budget code, course number, number of unique library subjects offered, minimum total units, the subject title with the most enrolled students for that course, and the corresponding number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1165\", \"desc\": \"For each subject where the responsible faculty MIT ID in the library subject offered table is 928034000 or the number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table is greater than 5, and where the offer department name in the tip subject offered table is either 'Chemistry' or 'Biology', show the subject title from the library subject offered table, the offer department name from the tip subject offered table, the term code from both tables, the number of enrolled students from both tables, and the minimum number of enrolled students in the tip subject offered table over each master subject ID group. Additionally, for the department offering the subject, show the department name, the range of enrolled students, and the variance of enrolled students in the subjects offered by that department, considering only departments that grant degrees, courses that are at the graduate level, and excluding the Biology department. Present the results ordered by subject title and department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1350\", \"desc\": \"For each department and school, provide the department name, school name, the average, range, and variance of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department, and the total enrolled students, considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with at least one enrolled student. Additionally, for each school, include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (null department name, school name, nulls for statistics, and total enrolled students). For students whose first name is 'Peter' and who are in the Mathematics department, also show their last name, email address, student year, and the minimum department budget code in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's full name, as well as the department full name and department last activity date. The results include all these columns in the following order: department name, school name, average enrolled students, range of enrolled students, variance of enrolled students, total enrolled students, last name, email address, student year, windowed minimum department budget code, department full name, and department last activity date. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1427\", \"desc\": \"For each course in the Mathematics department that is degree granting and has a course level of 'G', show the course description, department name, school name, the administrative department name, and the dense rank over the administrative department name ordered by the administrative department name. Additionally, for each administrative department name, include a grand total of the number of such courses in the format of (null, null, null, administrative department name, null, total courses). Also, show the minimum total units, the sum of lecture units, and the number of unique subjects for letter graded Mathematics department subjects offered in the Spring Term 2021, along with the department name and term description (with all other columns as null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3237\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of active graduate students with an office location assigned in that department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5187\", \"desc\": \"How many unique members with a non-null MIT ID are listed in MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL whose last update date is after January 1, 2015, whose department name in the employee directory contains the word \\\"Department\\\", and who are in the \\\"Political Science\\\" department (Course 17)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2559\", \"desc\": \"For each DLC whose DLC name contains the word 'Office', is not the biology department, and has at least one assignable organization, what are the DLC key, DLC name, the number of unique organizations, the total number of assignable organizations, the department name, the maximum organization number, the name of the space unit associated with that department, and the earliest warehouse load date among its organizations, considering only departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a maximum organization number greater than 50000 and excluding the \\\"Political Science\\\" department (Course 17)? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1689\", \"desc\": \"For each school, what is the school name and the highest average number of enrolled students per department (among its degree-granting departments, excluding Chemistry, and only considering subjects with at least one enrolled student), and for each subject offered by the Chemistry department in the 2019FA term that has course materials, what is the subject title, the dense rank of the subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the number of enrolled students descending, the full name of the offering department, and the school name of the Chemistry department? List the school name and highest average enrolled students per department first, followed by the Chemistry subject title, dense rank, department full name, and Chemistry school name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1033\", \"desc\": \"Show the department name, department full name, student full name, student email address, dense rank over the school code, CIP program code range, and CIP program code variance for all graduate students in degree-granting Mathematics departments, as well as for all Mathematics departments that are degree granting and have at least one course with a non-null CIP program code, including the CIP program code range and variance for those departments even if they have no such students. List the results ordered by department full name and student full name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3904\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name (from subject code), school name, the number of subject codes per school name and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'), and for each matching department in subjects offered in the term with code '2022SU', show the subject's ID, total units, department name (from subject offered), and their dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes, null, null, null, null). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4231\", \"desc\": \"For each department that both offered subjects in the current SIS term and is a degree-granting department that offered subjects in the term '2016SP', list the department code, offering department name, subject title, responsible faculty name, term description, academic year description, total number of subjects offered per department in the current term, department name, number of subjects offered in 2016SP, and total units for those subjects in 2016SP. Include all columns in the order: department code, offering department name, subject title, responsible faculty name, term description, academic year description, total number of subjects offered per department in the current term, department name, number of subjects offered in 2016SP, and total units for those subjects in 2016SP. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3163\", \"desc\": \"For each department name and course level where the course is degree granting and the total units are greater than 6, provide the number of unique courses, the minimum total units offered, and the number of courses where the design units are at least 3. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3294\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for academic term parameters where the term indicator is 'C', show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the term parameter, the term code, the academic year, and the running sum of academic years within each department ordered by academic year, for cases where the department matches in both sets. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3727\", \"desc\": \"For each department that is degree-granting and offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021, or for each department that offered more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, and the total number of tip materials. List the department code, department name, department full name, number of subjects offered, total number of enrolled students, and total number of tip materials in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3660\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, and for each subject offered in the term with the description \\\"Fall Term 2024-2025\\\" by the same department, show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the subject offered key, subject title, offering department name, the term description, and the rank of each subject within its offering department ordered by subject offered key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2759\", \"desc\": \"For each employee type and department name where the student year is 'G', show the number of people, the minimum MIT ID, and the list of unique office locations for those employees. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1474\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 degree-granting departments (excluding 'Political Science' and Course 17) that have offered at least one subject in the 'Engineering' school, list the department name, school name, subject code description, the total number of subjects they offered, and the average number of enrolled students per subject, and for each such department, show the full names, email addresses, student years, department full names, course descriptions, course levels, the minimum course level in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the student's last name, and the corresponding subject code and subject code description for each course taken by students named 'Kevin' in 'Electrical Eng & Computer Sci' (Course 6). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3901\", \"desc\": \"For each offer department code in the 2012SU term with total units greater than 0, list the subject title, course number, department name, the dense rank over the offer department code, the course, course description, school name, program code, program title, category code, category title, four digit code, four digit title, and the minimum warehouse load date from the CIP table over each category code group for courses in department 6, and include a grand total of subjects per offer department code and a grand total for all courses in each school in the format (nulls for subject-specific fields, department name, total subjects, course-specific fields, school name, and total courses). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3828\", \"desc\": \"For courses in the School of Engineering that are degree granting, show the course description, department name, the dense rank of each course considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the department's budget code, the subject code description, and the row number of each course within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by course description. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3498\", \"desc\": \"List all subject IDs that are either offered in the term with code '2025FA' or are offered in the term '2016SP' by departments that grant degrees, along with the subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department, and the dense rank considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the total number of units. For subjects from the term '2025FA', show the subject title, offering department name, number of enrolled students, term description, academic year, term start date, term end date, term parameter, and the minimum number of enrolled students over each offering department; for subjects from the term '2016SP' by degree-granting departments, show the dense rank as window_column. The results are ordered by subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1302\", \"desc\": \"For each course offered by a degree-granting department in the School of Engineering, except for the Electrical Engineering and Computer Science department, in the 2007 academic year, what is the course key, course name, department name, the number of catalog subjects, the total units for those subjects, and for each department, include a grand total for all courses in the format of (null, null, department name, total subjects, total units)? Additionally, for each such department, what is the total number of units for courses in the \\\"Engineering\\\" or \\\"Non-MIT\\\" schools (where the total units for the department is greater than 1000 and the department is not \\\"Political Science\\\"), and how many distinct courses did the department offer in the most recent academic year available? Present the results as: course key, course name, department name, number of catalog subjects, total units for those subjects, department total units, and number of distinct courses in the latest year, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4405\", \"desc\": \"For each combination of activity and department/academic year enrollment statistics, list the activity title, enrollment type, maximum enrollment, category name, category description, and the dense rank of each row partitioned by the category name and ordered by the category name, along with the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects offered (subject count), minimum number of total units for those subjects, and the average number of enrolled students per subject (for departments and academic years where the number of enrolled students in a subject is greater than 5). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1393\", \"desc\": \"For each academic year and department in Mathematics, what is the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered in that year and department (considering only subjects offered in the current term, with more than 0 total units, and with subject enrollment number greater than the average for that department and year), and for those departments, what are the department code, corresponding administrative department name, the graduate level of courses, and the total number of distinct courses per department, for all degree-granting departments except the Management department? Present the results as academic year, department name, total units variance, total units standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), department code, administrative department name, graduate level, and number of distinct courses, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4184\", \"desc\": \"For each department, show the offer department name, the number of distinct subjects offered by the department in the academic year 2012, and for each subject that was offered in the term \\\"2012SU\\\", display the subject key, subject title, academic year, term description, subject enrollment number, subject offered summary key, the average subject enrollment number within each subject key group, and the deviation of each subject's enrollment number from the average enrollment number for its subject key group, ordered by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2272\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department, what is the department name, the average of the total units, the range of the total units, the variance of the total units for courses with total units greater than 0, and for each course level, what is the number of unique students and the minimum CIP program code among their courses, considering only degree-granting departments? Additionally, for each course level, what is the average number of lecture units and the maximum number of lab units for Mathematics courses? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3356\", \"desc\": \"For the top 10 subject titles by the number of reserved library materials for subjects offered in the term '2009SP', what are the subject title, the offering department name, the variance and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the number of enrolled students in subjects offered by that department (considering only departments that grant degrees and subjects with a non-null subject code description), and the count of reserved materials? Please provide the subject title, the offering department name, the variance, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP), and the count of reserved materials, in that order. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4650\", \"desc\": \"For each degree-granting department that offered at least one subject in the School of Engineering in 2021 and has more than 10 tip materials for subjects in the School of Engineering during regular terms, provide the department code, department name, department full name, the number of subjects offered, the total number of enrolled students in those subjects, the total number of tip materials, the average number of enrolled students per subject (rounded to two decimal places), and the ratio of total enrolled students to total tip materials (rounded to two decimal places), listing the results in descending order of the average number of enrolled students per subject.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4683\", \"desc\": \"For each department where the total number of subject enrollments for subjects offered in the current term is greater than 10, and for each course number in that department where the number of enrolled students in the subject summary is greater than 2, provide the department name, the total number of subject enrollments, the course number, the number of unique library subjects offered, the minimum total units for those subjects, and the name of the responsible faculty member for each course. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_100\", \"desc\": \"Among all departments, which are the top 5 departments with the highest average office phone number among graduate students (student year 'G') who have a non-null office phone number? For each of these departments, show the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of office phone numbers, and the full name and office phone number of the graduate student in that department with the highest office phone number. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2398\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and the average number of enrolled students for each subject in the department, considering only subjects that are offered in the fall term and are not offered in the summer term. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4130\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2012 that also have a section ID of 0 and a cluster type of 'S', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, academic year, term description, the total number of subjects offered by each department in that year, the row number within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, the department name from SUBJECT_SUMMARY, the term start date from ACADEMIC_TERMS, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the subject title from SUBJECT_OFFERED. List the results in order by offer department name and subject key. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5377\", \"desc\": \"How many subjects offered in 2012 as part of the Harvard Cross-Enrollment Program, in either the Chemistry or Biology departments, had a total of more than 1 unit? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3078\", \"desc\": \"For each subject title and department name where the total units are greater than 3, give the number of offered sections, the minimum number of enrolled students, and the average lab units for those subjects. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_538\", \"desc\": \"For each HASS attribute, what is the range and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year by the Political Science department, along with the HASS attribute's description as shown on the form and the description in the bulletin? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4515\", \"desc\": \"For each department, academic year, activity title, and sponsor name where the subject enrollment number is greater than 10 and the maximum enrollment for the activity is greater than 10, provide the department name, academic year, number of unique subjects, minimum total units offered, activity title, sponsor name, number of unique activities, minimum fee, and the sponsor type. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1212\", \"desc\": \"For the Mathematics department (Course 18), provide the department name, the average and standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the total units for subjects offered by that department (considering only subjects with more than 0 total units and at least 1 enrolled student), the number of graduate students in the department, and the most recent warehouse load date for those students, considering only departments that are degree granting and students whose year is 'G'. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2580\", \"desc\": \"For each department and academic year, provide the department name, academic year, the number of subjects offered that are not repeatable for credit and are offered in the fall term, and classify the department as 'HIGH_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% more such subjects than the average across all departments for that year, 'LOW_ACTIVITY' if it offers at least 10% fewer, or 'AVERAGE' otherwise. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3452\", \"desc\": \"For organizations with an organization level of 5 and departments in the \\\"Provost Area\\\" with a non-null department code, show the organization name, organization ID, DLC name, HR org unit title, HR department name, HR org unit level, the row number within each HR department name group ordered by organization name, the department's long name, the corresponding hierarchy level 3 name from the master department hierarchy, and the row number within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by the department name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3911\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered by the library in the term with code '2014FA', show the subject ID, subject title, total number of enrolled students, offering department name, term description, term start date, term end date, and the minimum number of enrolled students for each offering department, as well as the maximum windowed average record count from tip detail records with material status key 'RQ' (using a window of 2 preceding and 2 following rows grouped by financial aid year). Additionally, for each offering department, include a grand total row showing the total number of enrolled students across all its subjects (with nulls for subject ID and subject title), and the corresponding maximum windowed average record count if available. Order the results by offering department name and subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4490\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting, show the subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, the number of subject codes per school name, and whether the subject code description is present ('Has Description') or missing ('No Description'). For each school name, include a grand total for all subject codes in the format of (null, null, null, school name, null, total subject codes). Additionally, for subjects offered in the term '2016SP' with a school code of 'E', show the subject title, course description, the offering department name, and assign row numbers within a window of 2 preceding and 1 following rows ordered by subject title. Present all columns in the following order: subject code, subject code description, department name, school name, description status, total subject codes, subject title, course description, offering department name, and window column. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_1465\", \"desc\": \"For each department in the Provost Area at the School of Science level, excluding the Biology department, and for each organization within those departments (excluding organizations with IDs '138' and '250'), show the department name, department code, organization name, organization ID, the maximum average organization number within each department code group, and the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the area of rooms assigned to the organization (considering only organizations with more than 5 rooms and excluding organizations named 'ADMISSIONS'), ordered by department name and organization name. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3635\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the academic year 2024 with a total of 12 units, and for subjects offered in the term 2019FA from the same department, show the subject code, subject number, subject title, department name, term description, the rank of each 2024 subject within its department ordered by subject code, the 2019FA subject ID, number of enrolled students in 2019FA, department full name, and the row number of each 2019FA subject within its department name group ordered by subject ID. Order the results by department name, subject code, and 2019FA subject ID. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3398\", \"desc\": \"For each subject offered in the same term as a TIP detail record with material status 'RQ', show the subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, and the rank of each record within each offer department name group ordered by subject key, along with the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key, where the subject, term, and offer department name match in both cases. List the columns in the following order: subject key, subject title, offer department name, TIP material key, rank, subject title (from the second subquery), subject ID, offer department name (from the second subquery), offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4756\", \"desc\": \"Show the department names, the corresponding SIS subject code, subject code descriptions, graduate level, the total number of courses per department, and for each department, the number of subjects offered in the academic year 2022 with a total of 12 units that also have at least one required or optional textbook. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_5103\", \"desc\": \"For subjects offered in the term '2017JA', show the subject title, the number of enrolled students, the responsible faculty name, the offering department name, the department full name, the school name, and the minimum number of enrolled students in a window of 3 preceding and 1 following row ordered by the department code. Additionally, for subjects offered in the term with code '2022FA' in the same department, provide the subject ID, department name, term description, the running sum of total units within each academic year ordered by subject ID, and the subject's short title and responsible faculty name from the course catalog. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_4234\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees and offered subjects in the term '2016SP', and is also among the top 5 offering departments in the 'Engineering' school with the most 12-unit courses, list the department code, department name, the number of subjects offered, the total units for those subjects, the offering department name, the number of qualifying 12-unit courses, and the course number and description of the most recently added 12-unit course in each department. For each department, also include a grand total row for the number of subjects and total units in the format (department code, null, total subjects, total units, ...). Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3042\", \"desc\": \"For each program category in the School of Engineering with a program version after 2000, what is the latest course start term, the highest program version, and the department that offers the most courses in that category, along with the count of courses from that department? Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_2224\", \"desc\": \"For each subject code where the department is degree granting and the department is Mathematics, and for each department that is degree granting and is not the Mathematics department (Course 18), show the subject code, subject code description, mathematics department name, school name, the average department budget code within each school, the administrative department name, the average clearing cost collector, the variance of the clearing cost collector, the standard deviation (using STDDEV only and never STDDEV_POP) of the clearing cost collector, and the most recent activity date for the administrative department. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}, {\"id\": \"dw_3277\", \"desc\": \"List all subject titles that are either (a) offered in the term '2022FA' with a total of 12 units, showing the subject title, department name from the course description, and the dense rank of each subject considering the current and 2 preceding rows ordered by the subject code from the course catalog, or (b) for each subject offered, show the subject title, subject ID, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and the maximum number of enrolled students for each subject considering the current row and the next 2 rows ordered by subject key. The results should include all these columns in the following order: subject title, department name, window column, offer department name, offer school name, term description, academic year, and maximum number of enrolled students, with NULLs for columns not relevant to each case. Do not return any rounded answers.\"}], \"concept\": [{\"id\": \"concept_department_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables describing academic departments and their school attribution: the SIS department dimension, the student-facing department lookup, and the SIS administrative department (contact information). They answer questions about department names, full names, school code/name, degree-granting status, budget codes, and department phone numbers, but differ in attribute coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing the institute's department/lab/center (DLC) and HR organization hierarchies: the HR organization unit dimension in two feed variants (HR_ORG_UNIT, HR_ORG_UNIT_NEW), the master department standard hierarchy path (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY), its DLC-to-administrative-object link table (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS), and the direct-parent department lookup (MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT). They jointly answer questions about which HR department/area a DLC or organization belongs to, the hierarchy path or parent of a department, and HR department names/codes/levels, and are joined to FCLT_ORGANIZATION via DLC_KEY for facilities/space attribution. They differ in hierarchy representation (full path vs direct parent vs HR unit attributes), unit coverage, and companion columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_person_directory\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing people of the institute keyed by MIT_ID: the primary employee directory (contact details, titles, HR department), the Drupal-sourced employee feed (employee group/type, appointment flags, HR org unit), the person master table (payroll rank, position title, active flag), the HR faculty roster (appointment type, terminal degree, emeritus status), the OPA current-person snapshot (HR job/appointment attributes, faculty flag, sabbatical), and the student directory (students with department attribution and student year). They jointly answer questions about who a person is, their contact details, job/appointment attributes, and whether they are employee, faculty, or student; responsible faculty in subject offering tables resolve to these tables via RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID = MIT_ID.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_subject_offering_facts\", \"desc\": \"Fact tables recording subjects offered per term from different business processes: the course catalog (planned catalog attributes), the registrar's section/subject offering records (actual sections and enrollment), subject-level summaries (final enrollment statistics), the textbook information program (subjects tracked for course materials), and library reserve processing (subjects with library reserve activity). They share subject identity (SUBJECT_ID, TERM_CODE) and department attribution but differ in granularity, enrollment semantics, and available measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_material_programs\", \"desc\": \"Tables covering course material provisioning: the Textbook Information Program (TIP) tracking textbook adoption status per subject offering, and library reserve processing tracking catalog items placed on reserve for subjects. They jointly answer questions about which subjects have course materials/textbooks, material status (TIP statuses such as 'RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options; library statuses such as 'U' Unknown, 'Y' Required Course Material), ISBNs, record counts, and reserve catalog item attributes. The two programs are linked by SUBJECT_ID + TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_course_catalog_sources\", \"desc\": \"Tables providing catalog-level subject attributes (titles, unit structure, grading rules, HGN level, requirement attributes, offering-term flags) from different source systems: the warehouse course catalog, the CIS course catalog feed, and the Drupal course catalog feed. They answer the same catalog-attribute questions but differ in source system, extra columns, and join paths to department/subject-code lookups.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_academic_term_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing academic terms and their calendar/status attributes. They jointly answer questions about when terms run, which academic/financial-aid/degree year a term belongs to, and whether a term is current, previous, future, or regular. Coverage differs: the full historical term list, the status-tracked term subset, and the three-row relative term parameter reference.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_time_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Time dimension tables of the warehouse at three granularities: TIME_DAY (one row per calendar date, with fiscal/calendar year and period, academic year, financial aid year, day of week, and the academic term code/description of the day), TIME_MONTH (one row per fiscal period in YYYYMM format, covering fiscal years 1996-2035, with fiscal quarter, calendar month, academic term, and financial aid year mappings), and TIME_QUARTER (one row per fiscal quarter, covering fiscal years 2000-2035, with quarter dates, payroll certification deadlines, and quarter status flags). They jointly answer questions about when fiscal periods/quarters/days run, which fiscal/calendar/academic year a date or month belongs to, and how day-level records roll up to months and quarters. They link to each other via FISCAL_PERIOD (day-month), FY_QUARTER_CODE (month-quarter), and FISCAL_YEAR (month-quarter association within the same fiscal year, fanning out months across all quarters of the year), and to the academic term tables via TIME_DAY.ACADEMIC_TERM_CODE or TIME_MONTH.ACADEMIC_TERM = TERM_CODE.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_facility_organization_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Organization dimension tables describing the institute's hierarchical organization tree used for facilities/space attribution: FCLT_ORGANIZATION (keyed by FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, with DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME) and FAC_ORGANIZATION (keyed by ORGANIZATION_KEY, with D_CODE). They answer the same questions about organization names, hierarchy levels, parent/major organizations, assignable flags, and HR cross-references, but belong to different table families and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_iap_activities\", \"desc\": \"Tables describing Independent Activities Period (IAP) activities offered in January terms: activity details (title, enrollment type, max enrollment, fee, cancellation flags), sessions (location, date, times), sponsors (name, type), categories, and persons. They jointly answer questions about IAP activity counts, enrollment capacity, fees, session scheduling, and sponsorship.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_cip_program_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables of the Classification of Instructional Programs (CIP) used to classify courses/instructional programs into two-digit categories, four-digit series, and six-digit program codes, with revision version years (1990/2000/2010/2020). CIP holds the current single-version classification (one row per program code, with a change NOTE), while CIP_WITH_VERSION preserves every revision of each program code across versions. Both join to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION via PROGRAM_CODE = CIP_PROGRAM_CODE to attribute courses to CIP programs and categories.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical building inventory and its attributes (number/name, type, ownership, site, campus sector, access level, gross/assignable/non-assignable areas, number of rooms, key dates): the current FCLT_* family snapshot, its fiscal-period history (in two date-format variants), the FAC_* family snapshot, and the lightweight space-domain building lookup. They jointly answer questions about building characteristics, areas, and room counts, but differ in time coverage, table family, attribute richness, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_major_use_classification\", \"desc\": \"Lookup tables classifying rooms by major use (classrooms, offices, laboratories, residential, circulation, etc.) with a short code, description, and assignable-space flag. They cover the current classification in the FCLT and FAC table families and the fiscal-period historical classification in the FCLT family, jointly answering questions about what a room is primarily used for and whether that use counts as assignable space.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_space_unit_dimension\", \"desc\": \"Space unit lookup tables identifying the organizational units that receive space allocation: SPACE_UNIT (with FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY organization attribution) and SPACE_UNIT2 (identity/name only). They answer the same space-unit identity questions but differ in organization linkage and coverage.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_moira_mailing_lists\", \"desc\": \"Tables of the Moira mailing-list/group domain: the list master (one row per list with name, description, active flag, and type flags such as mailing list, group, NFS group, public, hidden), the membership detail (one row per list member with member login, full name, MIT ID, and last update date), and the owner lookup (one row per owner entity with owner name and owner type LIST/USER/KERBEROS). They jointly answer questions about which lists exist and their properties, who belongs to a list, and who owns a list; MOIRA_LIST is the parent of MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_KEY, and MOIRA_LIST_OWNER is referenced by MOIRA_LIST_DETAIL via MOIRA_LIST_OWNER_KEY.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_building_address\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the postal/street addresses of buildings: the current FCLT_* family address table (multiple purpose-typed address rows per building), its fiscal-period historical counterpart, the FAC_* family address snapshot, and the single-text address fields of the space-domain BUILDINGS lookup. They jointly answer questions about where a building is located (street number/name, city, state, postal code), but differ in time coverage, address decomposition, and table family.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_room_space_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the physical room inventory and its space assignment: SPACE_DETAIL (rooms assigned to space units with usage classification and square footage), FCLT_ROOMS (facilities room inventory with use classifications, organization assignment, and area in square meters), FAC_ROOMS (the FAC_* family room snapshot with the same structure as FCLT_ROOMS but FAC_* keys), and ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD (space-planning room load feed with floor, space usage text, access level, and space unit code / HR org unit id links). They jointly answer questions about how many rooms exist, room sizes, room usage, and which organization/space unit occupies rooms, but differ in assignment perspective, key family, and area units.\"}, {\"id\": \"concept_floor_inventory\", \"desc\": \"Tables recording the floor level of buildings: the current FCLT_* family floor inventory with floor areas, the FAC_* family floor snapshot with the same structure, the fiscal-period historical floor table, and the lightweight space-domain floor lookup. They jointly answer questions about floor numbers and per-floor assignable/non-assignable areas, but differ in time coverage, table family, and attribute richness.\"}], \"column_concept\": [{\"id\": \"column_concept_department_name\", \"desc\": \"Department name columns across subject offering, catalog, lookup, employee, and library reserve instructor tables. Two academic naming conventions exist (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME) with the same academic value domain; LIBRARY_COURSE_INSTRUCTOR.DEPARTMENT also holds academic departments but in a 'COURSE_NUMBER - Department Name' prefixed format (e.g. '18 - Mathematics'); EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY.DEPARTMENT_NAME shares the column name but holds the HR organizational unit name (different value domain). Choosing the right one depends on the table family, the value format, whether the department is the catalog owner or the actual offering department, and whether an academic or HR department is meant.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_dlc_key\", \"desc\": \"Department/Lab/Center key columns (values like 'D_AEROASTRO', 'D_IDSS', 'D_BIOLOGY') identifying a DLC across the facilities, HR, space, and academic-department domains. They are the universal cross-domain join key linking facilities organizations and space units to HR organization units, the master department hierarchy, and academic departments. Naming and completeness vary: DLC_KEY in most tables, D_CODE in MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, DLC_CODE in the master hierarchy tables; some columns carry composite values ('D_DSL:HQ') or nulls.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_year_columns\", \"desc\": \"Year columns across term, catalog, and time dimension tables representing different year systems: academic year, fiscal year, financial aid year, and degree year. Selecting the correct year system is essential for yearly grouping and partitioning.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_type_site\", \"desc\": \"Building classification columns replicated across the current and historical building tables of both table families: BUILDING_TYPE ('ACADEMIC', 'SERVICE', 'RESIDENT') and SITE ('MIT', 'BATES', 'LINC', 'BOS', etc.). They carry the same value domain but differ in time semantics: the building-table columns are the current classification, while the history-table columns are the classification recorded at each fiscal period, so filtering by one versus the other can select different building sets.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_hass_attribute\", \"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code and description columns. The code columns appear in the three course catalog feeds and in the CIS_HASS_ATTRIBUTE lookup; description columns exist in three variants: the catalog-embedded HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC, the lookup's DESCRIPTION_ON_FORM (registration-form wording), and DESCRIPTION_IN_BULLETIN (short bulletin wording). Selecting the right description variant depends on the wording requested by the question.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_office_location\", \"desc\": \"OFFICE_LOCATION columns recording where a person's office/desk is, replicated across the person-directory tables (SE_PERSON, MIT_STUDENT_DIRECTORY, EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY, DRUPAL_EMPLOYEE_DIRECTORY). All hold a building or building-room text identifier in the same value domain as FCLT_ROOMS.BUILDING_ROOM, but they describe different populations (employee/person master vs student vs primary employee directory vs Drupal employee feed) and differ sharply in non-null coverage and in how many values are building-room ('BLDG-ROOM') versus building-only ('BLDG'). Choosing the right column determines whose office is reported and whether room-level joins to FCLT_ROOMS succeed.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_master_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Master subject identifier columns (MASTER_SUBJECT_ID and its sortable variant MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT) replicated across the registrar offering tables, the subject summary, the textbook program, the library reserve program, and the CIS course catalog. For clustered subjects (e.g. joint or cross-listed offerings), the master subject identifier points to the leading subject of the cluster, so joining on it matches offerings that share the same master subject even when their own SUBJECT_ID differs. SUBJECT_ID/SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the subject itself, while MASTER_SUBJECT_ID/MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT identify the cluster's master; the _SORT columns are the sortable forms of the same values used for cross-table joins.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_subject_id\", \"desc\": \"Subject identifier columns shared across catalog, registrar, textbook-program, and library tables. SUBJECT_ID is the cross-domain subject join key in 'CODE.NUMBER' format (e.g. '18.01'); it appears in every subject-related fact table but at different grains and program scopes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_term_code\", \"desc\": \"Term code columns in YYYYTT format (e.g. '2025FA', '2019SP', '2021JA', '2012SU'; TT = FA Fall, SP Spring, JA January/IAP, SU Summer) appearing across term dimension and fact tables. They are the universal join key linking subject offerings, textbook materials, library reserves, and IAP activities to term attributes.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_enrollment_measures\", \"desc\": \"Enrollment measure columns across subject offering, summary, textbook-program, and library tables. Two families exist: NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS (student headcount snapshots) and SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER (official registrar enrollment), at section, subject, or program scope.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_total_units\", \"desc\": \"Total credit unit columns replicated across catalog and registrar subject tables. They represent the same business quantity (total credit units of a subject) but come from different processes and pair with different companion unit columns.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_material_status_key\", \"desc\": \"Material status key columns of the textbook program (TIP) and library reserve program. Both are coded status references decoded by their own lookup tables (key value equals code value), with independent value domains: TIP statuses ('RQ' Required, 'EO' Electronic options, 'RC' Recommended, 'PC' Val-u option, 'BR' Bookstore recommends, 'CL' Go to class first, 'NM' Course has no materials, 'U' Unknown, plus NULL-description keys) vs library reserve statuses ('U' Unknown, 'R' null description, 'N' Non-Required Course Material, 'O' Reserve only, 'X' No Required Textbook, 'Y' Required Course Material).\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_access_level\", \"desc\": \"Access level columns recorded at three granularity levels of the facilities domain plus the space-planning room feed: building-level ACCESS_LEVEL_CODE/ACCESS_LEVEL_NAME (current and per-fiscal-period history), floor-level ACCESS_LEVEL, and room-level ACCESS_LEVEL (FCLT_ROOMS, FAC_ROOMS, ZPM_ROOMS_LOAD). They share a numeric value domain (observed 0-3) but describe the access restriction of different physical objects or come from different feeds, so filters and joins must target the granularity and table family the question refers to.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_space_unit_key\", \"desc\": \"Space unit key columns identifying the organizational space-assignment unit across the space dimension and fact tables. SPACE_UNIT_KEY is the join key linking SPACE_DETAIL room rows to space unit identity (name/code) and, through SPACE_UNIT, to the owning facilities organization.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_building_room\", \"desc\": \"Combined building-room identifier columns (e.g. '1-080') appearing in both the space assignment fact table and the facilities room inventory. They identify the same physical room concept but come from different business processes with different coverage and companion measures.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_fiscal_period\", \"desc\": \"Fiscal period code columns in YYYYMM format (e.g. '199602' = FY1996 period 2, '201505') appearing in two distinct roles: as the primary key of the month-grain time dimension (TIME_MONTH.FISCAL_PERIOD, also mirrored in TIME_DAY.FISCAL_PERIOD for day-to-month linkage), and as the snapshot-period stamp of the facilities historical tables (FCLT_BUILDING_HIST, FCLT_BUILDING_HIST_1, FCLT_BUILDING_ADDRESS_HIST, FCLT_FLOOR_HIST, FCLT_ROOMS_HIST, FCLT_MAJOR_USE_HIST). Both roles share the same YYYYMM value domain, but the time dimension uses it for calendar grouping while the history tables use it to mark when a facilities snapshot was taken.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_facility_organization_key\", \"desc\": \"Facility organization key columns attributing space units and rooms to organizations in the hierarchical organization tree. Two naming conventions exist across table families (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY in FCLT_*/SPACE_* tables vs ORGANIZATION_KEY in FAC_* tables) with the same value domain.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_assignable_area\", \"desc\": \"Assignable-area measure columns at different granularity levels and time semantics: building-level current and per-fiscal-period assignable area, floor-level assignable area, and the space-domain assignable square footage. All FCLT_*/FAC_* columns are in square meters; BUILDINGS.BLDG_ASSIGNABLE_SQUARE_FOOTAGE is in square feet. Choosing the right column determines whether the measure is a building total, a floor total, a historical value, or a space-assignment figure.\"}, {\"id\": \"column_concept_num_of_rooms\", \"desc\": \"NUM_OF_ROOMS columns recording how many rooms a building contains, replicated across the current and historical building tables of both families. The building-table columns hold the current room count (one value per building); the history-table columns hold the room count at each fiscal period, used for room-count statistics (average, range, variance, minimum) across a building's history records.\"}]}}"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "tool_calls": [
        {
          "id": "call_7e54d5cb770143b7adde80e9",
          "type": "function",
          "function": {
            "name": "semantic_get",
            "arguments": "{\"entity_ids\": \n[\"dw_2151\", \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\"]\n\n}"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "role": "tool",
      "tool_call_id": "call_7e54d5cb770143b7adde80e9",
      "name": "semantic_get",
      "content": "{\"ok\": true, \"entities\": [{\"category\": \"Course Catalog and Department Analysis\", \"default_granularity\": \"one row per degree-granting department matched with Political Science HGN statistics\", \"desc\": \"For each department that grants degrees (excluding the Biology department), provide the department name, the average and variance of the total units for subjects offered by that department in the 2022 academic year, and, if the department is Political Science, also include for each HGN code the maximum number of lecture units among all subjects in the course catalog and the subject title from the subject offered table for subjects offered in the year 2012 with more than 2 lecture units, as well as the number of enrolled students for those subjects. List the results ordered by the variance of total units in descending order, and for Political Science, by the maximum lecture units in descending order. Do not return any rounded answers.\", \"id\": \"dw_2151\", \"name\": \"Degree-Granting Department 2022 Unit Average-Variance with Political Science HGN Lecture Unit Maximums\", \"sql\": \"WITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(s.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_units, VARIANCE(s.TOTAL_UNITS) AS units_variance FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT d JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED s ON d.DEPARTMENT_CODE = s.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE s.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND d.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND d.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '7' GROUP BY d.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY units_variance DESC ) , PoliSciHGNStats AS ( SELECT c.HGN_CODE, c.DEPARTMENT_NAME, MAX(c.LECTURE_UNITS) AS max_lecture_units, s.SUBJECT_TITLE, so.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS FROM COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED c JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED s ON c.HGN_CODE = s.HGN_CODE JOIN SUBJECT_OFFERED so ON s.SUBJECT_KEY = so.SUBJECT_KEY WHERE c.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2012 AND c.LECTURE_UNITS > 2 AND c.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Political Science' GROUP BY c.HGN_CODE, c.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.SUBJECT_TITLE, so.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS HAVING MAX(c.LECTURE_UNITS) > 2 ) SELECT d.DEPARTMENT_NAME, d.avg_units, d.units_variance, p.HGN_CODE, p.max_lecture_units, p.SUBJECT_TITLE, p.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS FROM inner_cte d LEFT JOIN PoliSciHGNStats p ON d.DEPARTMENT_NAME = p.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY d.units_variance DESC, p.max_lecture_units DESC\"}, {\"id\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"name\": \"COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\", \"desc\": \"Course catalog subject offering table recording catalog-level attributes of each subject offered per academic year and term: subject identity (SUBJECT_ID = SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_NUMBER), department, unit structure (lecture/lab/preparation/design/total units), grading type and rules, HGN level (Undergraduate/Graduate/High Graduate), requirement attributes (GIR, HASS, communication, writing), term offering flags (this year, fall, IAP, spring, summer), instructors, section flags, responsible faculty, and meeting time/place. Links to terms via both TERM_CODE (the offering term) and EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE (the term from which catalog attributes take effect).\", \"columns\": {\"ACADEMIC_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year of the catalog offering, e.g. 2022\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code of the offering record in YYYYTT format; joins to term tables\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier formed as SUBJECT_CODE + '.' + SUBJECT_NUMBER, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, SUBJECT_SUMMARY subject IDs\"}, \"SUBJECT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject/course code prefix, e.g. '18' for Mathematics; joins to SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE and SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.SUBJECT_CODE\"}, \"SUBJECT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Subject number within the subject code, e.g. '01'\"}, \"SOURCE_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Source system subject identifier\"}, \"PRINT_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier as printed in the bulletin\"}, \"IS_PRINTED_IN_BULLETIN\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is printed in the bulletin\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department name, e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"}, \"EFFECTIVE_TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code from which the catalog attributes of this subject take effect; frequently joined to ACADEMIC_TERMS.TERM_CODE for term-status filtering\"}, \"SUBJECT_SHORT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Short title of the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Full title of the subject\"}, \"IS_VARIABLE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject has variable units\"}, \"LECTURE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of lecture credit units\"}, \"LAB_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of lab credit units\"}, \"PREPARATION_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of preparation (outside-class) credit units\"}, \"TOTAL_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Total credit units of the subject (lecture+lab+preparation unless variable)\"}, \"DESIGN_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of design credit units\"}, \"GRADE_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Grade type code, e.g. 'L' = letter graded\"}, \"GRADE_TYPE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Grade type description\"}, \"GRADE_RULE\": {\"desc\": \"Grade rule code\"}, \"GRADE_RULE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Grade rule description, e.g. 'Not repeatable for credit'\"}, \"HGN_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"HGN (Higgins) level code\"}, \"HGN_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HGN level description: 'Undergraduate', 'Graduate', or 'High Graduate'\"}, \"HGN_EXCEPT\": {\"desc\": \"HGN exception indicator\"}, \"GIR_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"General Institute Requirement attribute code\"}, \"GIR_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"General Institute Requirement attribute description\"}, \"COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Communication requirement attribute code\"}, \"COMM_REQ_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Communication requirement attribute description\"}, \"TUITION_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Tuition attribute code\"}, \"TUITION_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Tuition attribute description\"}, \"WRITE_REQ_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Writing requirement attribute code\"}, \"WRITE_REQ_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Writing requirement attribute description\"}, \"SUPERVISOR_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"Supervisor attribute code\"}, \"SUPERVISOR_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Supervisor attribute description\"}, \"PREREQUISITES\": {\"desc\": \"Prerequisite text for the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Full catalog description text of the subject\"}, \"JOINT_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"List of joint subjects\"}, \"SCHOOL_WIDE_ELECTIVES\": {\"desc\": \"School-wide elective attribute\"}, \"MEETS_WITH_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Subjects this one meets with\"}, \"EQUIVALENT_SUBJECTS\": {\"desc\": \"Equivalent subjects\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_THIS_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the current academic year\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_FALL_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the fall term\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_IAP\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered during IAP (January)\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_SPRING_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the spring term\"}, \"IS_OFFERED_SUMMER_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the subject is offered in the summer term\"}, \"FALL_INSTRUCTORS\": {\"desc\": \"Fall term instructor names\"}, \"SPRING_INSTRUCTORS\": {\"desc\": \"Spring term instructor names\"}, \"STATUS_CHANGE\": {\"desc\": \"Catalog status change indicator\"}, \"LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the record\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier when the subject is part of a cluster\"}, \"HASS_ATTRIBUTE\": {\"desc\": \"HASS (Humanities, Arts, and Social Sciences) attribute code\"}, \"HASS_ATTRIBUTE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HASS attribute description\"}, \"TERM_DURATION\": {\"desc\": \"Duration of the subject within the term\"}, \"GLOBAL_REGIONS\": {\"desc\": \"Global regions associated with the subject\"}, \"GLOBAL_COUNTRIES\": {\"desc\": \"Global countries associated with the subject\"}, \"ON_LINE_PAGE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Online catalog page number\"}, \"SECTION_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Section identifier of the subject offering\"}, \"IS_MASTER_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for master section\"}, \"IS_LECTURE_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for lecture section\"}, \"IS_LAB_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for lab section\"}, \"IS_RECITATION_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for recitation section\"}, \"IS_DESIGN_SECTION\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag for design section\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the faculty member responsible for the subject\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"MIT ID of the responsible faculty member\"}, \"MEET_TIME\": {\"desc\": \"Meeting time text of the subject\"}, \"MEET_PLACE\": {\"desc\": \"Meeting place; stores the FCLT room key and joins to FCLT_ROOMS.FCLT_ROOM_KEY for facility/space analysis\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject offering per term/academic year\"}, {\"id\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"name\": \"SIS_DEPARTMENT\", \"desc\": \"SIS department dimension table: academic departments with code, name, full name, school attribution (code and name), budget code, degree-granting flag, and commencement-book names. Joins to subject offering tables via department codes.\", \"columns\": {\"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department code; joins to offering tables' DEPARTMENT_CODE/OFFER_DEPT_CODE and SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name, e.g. 'Mathematics', 'Chemistry'\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_FULL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Full official name of the department\"}, \"SCHOOL_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"School code the department belongs to, e.g. 'E'\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"School name the department belongs to, e.g. 'Engineering'; used for school-level filtering\"}, \"DEPT_BUDGET_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Budget code of the department; used for budget-based ordering/ranking\"}, \"IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag whether the department is degree granting\"}, \"DEPT_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"Department name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME_IN_COMMENCEMENT_BK\": {\"desc\": \"School name as printed in the commencement book\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME_HISTORY\": {\"desc\": \"Historical names of the department\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_LAST_ACTIVITY_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Date of last activity on the department record\"}, \"DLC_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Degree-granting list/committee key\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic department\"}, {\"id\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"name\": \"ACADEMIC_TERMS\", \"desc\": \"Academic term dimension table describing each academic term's calendar and status attributes: term code/description, start/end dates, academic year, financial aid year, degree year, key registration and class dates, and term status classification (Previous/Current/Future, regular vs non-regular term). Used to filter and enrich subject offerings by term characteristics.\", \"columns\": {\"ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the academic term record; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL.ACADEMIC_TERMS_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format, e.g. '2025FA' (FA=Fall, SP=Spring, JA=January/IAP, SU=Summer)\"}, \"TERM_DESCRIPTION\": {\"desc\": \"Human-readable term description, e.g. 'Fall Term 2024-2025'\"}, \"TERM_SELECTOR\": {\"desc\": \"Term selector label used for picklists\"}, \"TERM_START_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Term start date; can match TIME_DAY.CALENDAR_DATE for calendar-based joins\"}, \"TERM_END_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Term end date\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year the term belongs to, e.g. 2025\"}, \"ACADEMIC_YEAR_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Academic year description text\"}, \"IS_CURRENT_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag indicating whether the term is the current term\"}, \"IS_REGULAR_TERM\": {\"desc\": \"'Y'/'N' flag indicating a regular term (Fall/Spring) versus non-regular terms (Summer, January/IAP); only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS, not in ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"TERM_STATUS_INDICATOR\": {\"desc\": \"Single-character term status indicator: 'P'=Previous, 'C'=Current, 'F'=Future, 'None'=Unspecified\"}, \"TERM_STATUS\": {\"desc\": \"Term status text: 'Previous', 'Current', 'Future', or 'Unspecified'\"}, \"FINANCIAL_AID_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Financial aid year the term maps to\"}, \"DEGREE_YEAR\": {\"desc\": \"Degree year the term maps to; used in degree-year statistics\"}, \"LAST_DAY_OF_FINAL_EXAM\": {\"desc\": \"Last day of final exams for the term\"}, \"PRE_REGISTRATION_START_DAY\": {\"desc\": \"First day of pre-registration for the term\"}, \"REGISTRATION_DAY\": {\"desc\": \"Registration day for the term\"}, \"FIRST_DAY_OF_CLASSES\": {\"desc\": \"First day of classes in the term\"}, \"LAST_DAY_OF_CLASSES\": {\"desc\": \"Last day of classes in the term\"}, \"ADD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Last day to add a subject in the term; only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS\"}, \"DROP_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Last day to drop a subject in the term; only present in ACADEMIC_TERMS\"}, \"GRADUATE_AWARD_START_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"Start date of the graduate award period for the term\"}, \"GRADUATE_AWARD_END_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"End date of the graduate award period for the term\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date of the record\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per academic term\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level summary fact table per term: one row per subject (or cluster) per term with department/school attribution, unit structure (total/lecture/lab/prep/design units), and detailed enrollment statistics including final enrollment, first-week and fifth-week enrollment, and credit/listener splits at both subject and cluster level. Used for enrollment and unit statistics by department, school, term, and subject group.\", \"columns\": {\"SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the subject summary record\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL, LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED subject IDs\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the subject identifier\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject title\"}, \"SUBJECT_OR_CLUSTER\": {\"desc\": \"Indicator whether the row represents a subject or a cluster\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier for clustered subjects\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master subject identifier\"}, \"ULT_MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Ultimate master subject identifier in cluster hierarchies\"}, \"CLUSTER_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster type code\"}, \"CLUSTER_TYPE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster type description\"}, \"CLUSTER_LIST\": {\"desc\": \"List of subjects in the cluster\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"DEPARTMENT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Department name, e.g. 'Mathematics'\"}, \"SCHOOL_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"School code, e.g. 'E' for Engineering\"}, \"SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"School name, e.g. 'Engineering'\"}, \"TOTAL_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Total credit units of the subject\"}, \"LECTURE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lecture credit units\"}, \"LAB_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lab credit units\"}, \"PREP_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Preparation credit units (named PREP_UNITS here vs PREPARATION_UNITS in other tables)\"}, \"DESIGN_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Design credit units\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Final enrollment number of the subject\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Final enrollment number of the cluster\"}, \"SUBJECT_GROUP_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject group identifier used for grouping related subjects\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_FIRST_WEEK\": {\"desc\": \"Subject enrollment in the first week\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_FIRST_WEEK\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster enrollment in the first week\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_FIFTH_WEEK\": {\"desc\": \"Subject enrollment in the fifth week\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_FIFTH_WEEK\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster enrollment in the fifth week\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_CREDIT\": {\"desc\": \"Number of students enrolled in the subject for credit\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_LISTEN\": {\"desc\": \"Number of listeners enrolled in the subject\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_CREDIT\": {\"desc\": \"Number of students enrolled in the cluster for credit\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_LISTEN\": {\"desc\": \"Number of listeners enrolled in the cluster\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_1ST_CREDIT\": {\"desc\": \"First-year/first-level credit enrollment of the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_1ST_LISTEN\": {\"desc\": \"First-year/first-level listener enrollment of the subject\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_1ST_CREDIT\": {\"desc\": \"First-year/first-level credit enrollment of the cluster\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_1ST_LISTEN\": {\"desc\": \"First-year/first-level listener enrollment of the cluster\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_5TH_CREDIT\": {\"desc\": \"Fifth-year/level credit enrollment of the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_5TH_LISTEN\": {\"desc\": \"Fifth-year/level listener enrollment of the subject\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_5TH_CREDIT\": {\"desc\": \"Fifth-year/level credit enrollment of the cluster\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_5TH_LISTEN\": {\"desc\": \"Fifth-year/level listener enrollment of the cluster\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject per term\"}, {\"id\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"name\": \"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY\", \"desc\": \"Subject-level rollup of section offerings per term: one row per subject offered in a term with unit structure (total/lecture/lab/preparation units), offering department and school, responsible faculty, cluster information, and enrollment numbers. Parent of SUBJECT_OFFERED (section level) via COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY.\", \"columns\": {\"SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Surrogate key of the subject offered summary record\"}, \"COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Composite subject key; joins to SUBJECT_OFFERED.COMPOSITE_SUBJECT_KEY\"}, \"TERM_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Term code in YYYYTT format; joins to ACADEMIC_TERMS/ACADEMIC_TERMS_ALL\"}, \"COURSE_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Course number of the subject; joins to SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER and SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Subject identifier, e.g. '18.01'; joins to TIP_DETAIL.SUBJECT_ID and LIBRARY_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_ID\"}, \"SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the subject identifier\"}, \"SUBJECT_TITLE\": {\"desc\": \"Subject title\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"Master subject identifier for clustered subjects\"}, \"MASTER_SUBJECT_ID_SORT\": {\"desc\": \"Sortable form of the master subject identifier\"}, \"CLUSTER_TYPE\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster type code\"}, \"CLUSTER_TYPE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"Cluster type description\"}, \"CLUSTER_LIST\": {\"desc\": \"List of subjects in the cluster\"}, \"HGN_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"HGN (Higgins) level code\"}, \"HGN_CODE_DESC\": {\"desc\": \"HGN level description\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_CODE\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department code; joins to SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\"}, \"OFFER_DEPT_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering department name\"}, \"OFFER_SCHOOL_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Offering school name, e.g. 'Engineering'; used for school-level filtering\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_NAME\": {\"desc\": \"Name of the faculty member responsible for the subject\"}, \"RESPONSIBLE_FACULTY_MIT_ID\": {\"desc\": \"MIT ID of the responsible faculty member\"}, \"TOTAL_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Total credit units of the subject\"}, \"LECTURE_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lecture credit units\"}, \"LAB_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Lab credit units\"}, \"PREPARATION_UNITS\": {\"desc\": \"Preparation credit units\"}, \"SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Enrollment number at the subject level\"}, \"CLUSTER_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER\": {\"desc\": \"Enrollment number of the cluster\"}, \"WAREHOUSE_LOAD_DATE\": {\"desc\": \"ETL warehouse load date\"}, \"NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\": {\"desc\": \"Number of students enrolled in the subject\"}, \"SUBJECT_GROUPING_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Key to the subject grouping record\"}, \"SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY\": {\"desc\": \"Foreign key to SUBJECT_SUMMARY.SUBJECT_SUMMARY_KEY\"}}, \"default_granularity\": \"one row per subject per term\"}], \"not_found\": []}"
